#: src/Service/NumberPattern.php:229
msgid "\"{DD}\" may only be used directly after \"{MM}\"."
msgstr "\"{DD}\" may only be used directly after \"{MM}\"."

#: src/Service/NumberPattern.php:237
msgid "A pattern using a date placeholder must start with \"{YY}\" or \"{YYYY}\", otherwise the numbers would repeat every year."
msgstr "A pattern using a date placeholder must start with \"{YY}\" or \"{YYYY}\", otherwise the numbers would repeat every year."

#: templates/pages/config.html.twig:93
msgid "A ticket number is the numeric id of the ticket, so the pattern may only produce digits. Fixed digits are allowed at the beginning, date placeholders must follow from the largest to the smallest unit, and the pattern ends with the \"#\" counter."
msgstr "A ticket number is the numeric id of the ticket, so the pattern may only produce digits. Fixed digits are allowed at the beginning, date placeholders must follow from the largest to the smallest unit, and the pattern ends with the \"#\" counter."

#: templates/pages/config.html.twig:187
msgid "Active pattern"
msgstr "Active pattern"

#: templates/pages/config.html.twig:238
msgid "An existing ticket already has a higher id than the start of this block. A ticket id can only ever grow, so this pattern cannot take effect until the counter reaches it."
msgstr "An existing ticket already has a higher id than the start of this block. A ticket id can only ever grow, so this pattern cannot take effect until the counter reaches it."

#: templates/pages/config.html.twig:157
msgid "Click an example to copy it into the pattern field. Nothing is saved until you press Save."
msgstr "Click an example to copy it into the pattern field. Nothing is saved until you press Save."

